From 691695d1ee4b0d266eca3a7f34e7463233db1c92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mitzev <ogi@kunasystems.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Apr 2026 01:02:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] P09.46: built-in attribute macro for #[swift_value] (1.02 #2)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Promotes the `swift_value!` proc-macro from crates/rustcc_macros
into a built-in attribute macro in rustc_builtin_macros. Users
now write `#[swift_value]` as a sibling of `#[swift_type = "..."]`
on a bare struct; the compiler synthesizes `#[repr(swift)]` (if
not already present), the metadata accessor `extern "C"` decl
with Swift-mangled link_name, `impl Drop` forwarding to
rustcc_swift_rt::drop_swift_value / release_swift_class, and
`impl Clone` forwarding to clone_swift_value (value types) or
a per-field-clone struct literal (class types with non-POD
extras — keeps the P09.42 semantics).

Files touched:
- compiler/rustc_builtin_macros/src/swift_value.rs (new,
  ~270 LOC): parses #[swift_type] as sibling attr, formats the
  expansion as Rust source, parses it via
  rustc_parse::new_parser_from_source_str, returns the
  augmented struct + synthesized items.
- compiler/rustc_builtin_macros/src/lib.rs: `swift_value:
  swift_value::expand` in the register_attr! list + `mod
  swift_value;`.
- compiler/rustc_span/src/symbol.rs: +swift_value symbol.
- library/core/src/macros/mod.rs: `pub macro swift_value($item:item)`
  stub with #[rustc_builtin_macro] so the resolver wires the
  expander; feature-gated behind rustc_attrs for now.
- library/core/src/prelude/v1.rs and
  library/std/src/prelude/v1.rs: re-export swift_value so users
  don't need a `use` statement (matches #[global_allocator]).

User-facing delta:
  before (P09.42):                      after (P09.46):
    rustcc_macros::swift_value! {         #[swift_value]
        #[swift_type = "Foo.Bar"]         #[swift_type = "Foo.Bar"]
        pub struct Bar { ... }            pub struct Bar { ... }
    }

The rustcc_macros proc macro can be deleted in a follow-up; for
now it still works (users on a prior-stage rustc keep the same
path). The new form additionally doesn't require importing
rustcc_macros — the attribute is in the prelude.

Validation:
- /tmp/p09-46-swift-value-attr/ probe: class-backed Bar with
  non-POD Box<i32> extra clones + drops without aliasing; value-
  type Point compiles/links (runtime would need a real Swift
  stdlib).
- Stage-1 library rebuilds clean.
- cargo test --workspace in rustcc repo: 235/0 (unchanged).
- fork/tests/run.sh: 5/5 (all prior class probes still pass).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
